  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There has been some change to the way that the personal mirror renders when turning off the environment toggle (putting it in \"cutout mode\"), causing it to look broken in several cases.\nIn the included pictures some of the following can be seen:\n- The transparent shader on these glasses renders with darker/inverted colours in the mirror.\n- Some clothes appear semi transparent in the mirror.\n- Some toggleables are fully transparent in the mirror. (The sweater is just completely gone)\nI've noticed similar issues with reflections of transparent/toggleable components of avatars overlapping with certain world components like video players and meshes with strong emissions. \nThese issues did not occur for me on an earlier version of the beta with these same avatars.",
